# Review Ready — Cursor Activation Rule

When the user is editing or working with mobile app configuration files (iOS or Android), Review Ready's audit tools are available.

## Available skills

- `/review-ready:scan` — Full pre-submission audit. Spawns 5 parallel subagents to check privacy compliance, IAP enforcement, permissions, metadata, and crash risk. Outputs a severity-ranked report with file:line references.
- `/review-ready:precheck` — Fast 30-second top-10 blocker check before submission.
- `/review-ready:fix` — Auto-applies safe compliance fixes from the latest scan.

## When to suggest these commands

Suggest a scan when the user:
- Mentions submitting to the App Store, Play Store, TestFlight, or EAS Build
- Asks about App Store rejections, Apple guidelines, Google Play policies
- Edits permission strings, privacy manifest, or app metadata
- Asks "will my app get rejected" / "is my app ready" / "check my app"

## Plugin location

The plugin lives at this repository. Skills are in `skills/`, subagent prompts are in `agents/`, store rule knowledge bases are in `rules/`, and real-world rejection examples are in `rules/real-rejections.md`.

## Hooks

When the user edits `Info.plist`, `AndroidManifest.xml`, `app.json`, `PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy`, `eas.json`, or `*.entitlements`, the plugin's hook fires a contextual compliance reminder.
